    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0472" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.6112/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 215.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 664
                    of March 22 last in which you enclose a copy and translation of Decree No. 83,
                    reviving the Zapata concession upon terms which, you state, seem to remove the
                    Department’s previous objections.</p>
                <p>In reply I enclose a copy of the Department’s letter of today’s date to Mr. Isaac
                    K. Champion, President of the Zapata Land Company.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For <signed>Mr. Bryan</signed>: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d310-a1.xml" xpointer="d310-a1"/>
            </div>
